  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Zaki Khan vs State Of U.P. And Another on 8 December, 2020 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth",
    "facts": "The instant Anticipatory Bail Application has been filed with a prayer to grant an anticipatory bail to the applicant, namely, Zaki Khan, in Case Crime No. 79 of 2020, under Sections 272,273, 420, 467, 468, 471 I.P.C and Section 63/65 of Copy Right Act and Section 60(A) of Excise Act , Police Station - Rasoolabad, District - Kanpur Dehat (Ramabai Nagar). Submission is that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under sections 272, 273, 420, 467, 468, 471 .P.C. is unjustified. Offence under section 60(A) of Excise Act is bailable and triable by Magistrate. False recovery has been alleged. Learned AGA has opposed the prayer for anticipatory bail of the applicant.",
    "arguments": "Without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case and considering the nature of accusation and his antecedents, the applicant is entitled to be released on anticipatory bail for limited period in this case considering the exceptions considered by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in the case of Sushila Aggarwal vs. State (NCT of Delhi)- 2020 SCC Online SC 98 and order dated 22.05.2020 passed by this Court in Criminal Misc. Anticipatory Bail Application No.2609 of 2020.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case and considering the nature of accusation and his antecedents, the applicant is entitled to be released on anticipatory bail for limited period in this case considering the exceptions considered by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in the case of Sushila Aggarwal vs. State (NCT of Delhi)- 2020 SCC Online SC 98 and order dated 22.05.2020 passed by this Court in Criminal Misc. Anticipatory Bail Application No.2609 of 2020."
